The '''Xunta Nacionalista''' ({{Literal translation|Nationalist Junta}}), fully and officially called the '''Free and Independent Bayaran Republic''' ({{langx|an|Republica Libre y Independient de Bayaran}}), was a ''[[W:De facto|de facto]]'' state that seceded from the [[Southern Confederation]] and roughly coincided with the present communities of [[Bayara]] and [[Estuaria]]. The Xunta's renunciation of the [[Articles of Confederation]] and withdrawal from the confederation was proclaimed on 6 July 1828, as a direct response to declaration of the [[Carpinchera Republic]]. It was recognised only by the [[W:Empire of Brazil|Empire of Brazil]].

